WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.410
We measured the heights of sixty

2
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:03.910
pupils for the health check.

3
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.250
Sixty numbers in a long list.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.160
Nobody could see anything in them.

5
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.540
So we drew their shape.

6
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.150
Today: how a histogram shows

7
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.450
the shape of your data.

8
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.580
A distribution tells you how

9
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.380
often each value happens.

10
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.310
Are most pupils near the middle height?

11
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.200
Are there many very tall or

12
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.340
very short pupils?

13
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.150
That is the shape of the data.

14
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:34.890
A histogram groups the

15
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.410
values into equal bins.

16
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.170
Here each bin is five centimetres wide:

17
00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.790
one forty to one forty five, one forty

18
00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.010
five to one fifty, and so on.

19
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.060
Then we count how many

20
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.660
pupils fall in each bin.

21
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.400
Each bar is one bin, and its

22
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.500
height is the count.

23
00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:58.220
Our bars rise to a peak in the middle and

24
00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.700
fall away on both sides, like a hill.

25
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.100
A shape like this is called symmetric.

26
00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.910
The two sides look alike, so the mean

27
00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.730
and the median are almost the same.

28
00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.570
Heights, shoe sizes and many

29
00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.250
test marks look like this.

30
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.160
Journey times look different.

31
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.980
Most pupils live close, but a

32
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.420
few travel for an hour.

33
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.520
The bars bunch on the left with

34
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.980
a long tail to the right.

35
00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.690
This is skewed right, and the tail

36
00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.030
pulls the mean above the median.

37
00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:35.750
Quick check!

38
00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.430
The journey times are skewed right.

39
00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.740
Which middle describes a

40
00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.820
typical pupil better?

41
00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:43.550
The median.

42
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.110
The few long journeys pull the

43
00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.330
mean up, so the mean is longer

44
00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.890
than most pupils' journeys.

45
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.470
The median stays with the typical pupil.

46
00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.180
In the app, open Build a histogram.

47
00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.830
Change the bin width from one to twenty.

48
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.860
Too few bins hide the hill, and

49
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.880
too many make a jagged comb.

50
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:07.700
Your turn.

51
00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.990
In a histogram of test marks, what

52
00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:12.530
does the height of each bar show?

53
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.250
How many pupils got marks in that bin.

54
00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:21.030
Remember: equal bins, bars that count, and

55
00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.690
a shape that is symmetric or skewed.

56
00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.880
The shape tells you which middle to trust.

57
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.280
Try it yourself: measure the hand

58
00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.140
spans of your family or friends,

59
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.040
and put them in equal bins.

60
00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.200
Draw the histogram and ask: is it a

61
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.140
hill, or does it have a tail?
